=== SCREENING TASK: Study 49 ===

SELECTION CRITERIA:
Study design: randomised controlled trial (RCT); Population: adults (>=18 years) with heart failure; Intervention: 
mHealth-delivered education (mobile and wireless technologies for health) such as internet/web-based education 
programmes for smartphones/tablets (including apps), SMS messages, social media-delivered education programmes; 
Comparison: usual HF care.

STUDY TITLE:
Telehealth for "the digital illiterate"--elderly heart failure patients experiences

STUDY ABSTRACT:
Telehealth solutions should be available also for elderly patients with no interest in using, or capacity to use, 
computers and smartphones. Fourteen elderly, severely ill heart failure patients in home care participated in a 
telehealth study and used digital pens for daily reporting of their health state--a technology never used before by this
patient group. After the study seven patients and two spouses were interviewed face-to-face. A qualitative content 
analysis of the interview material was performed. The informants had no experience of computers or the Internet and no 
interest in learning. Still, patients found the digital pen and the health diary form easy to use, thus effortlessly 
adopting to changes in care provision. They experienced an improved contact with the caregivers and had a sense of 
increased security despite a multimorbid state. Our study shows that, given that technologies are tailored to specific 
patient groups, even "the digital illiterate" may use the Internet.

INSTRUCTIONS: Based on the selection criteria above, decide whether this study should be INCLUDED or EXCLUDED. Provide a
brief rationale tied to specific criteria.


Out: None
