the augmented interventions greatly increased the practice of evidence-based care, according to patient records, in the 
areas of patient assessment and instructions about HF disease management. While not all results were statistically 
significant at conventional levels, intervention effects were positive in virtually all cases and effect magnitudes 
frequently were large. CONCLUSIONS The results of this randomized trial strongly support the efficacy of just-in-time 
evidence-based reminders as a means of changing clinical practice among home health nurses who are geographically 
