Decision: EXCLUDE
Rationale: The study is a randomised controlled trial of mobile phone-based telemonitoring in adult heart failure 
patients.
The intervention consists of daily weight, blood pressure, and weekly single-lead ECG measurements, plus daily symptom
questions answered on a mobile phone. Data are transmitted wirelessly to servers, and instructions are sent back
to the patients' phones, with alerts to a cardiologist. This constitutes a telemonitoring and management system,
not an mHealth-delivered education programme. The selection criteria specify mHealth education interventions such as
internet/web-based education programmes, smartphone/tablet apps, SMS messages, or social media-delivered education.
