BACKGROUND Coping Effectively with Heart Failure (COPE-HF) is an ongoing randomized clinical trial funded by the 
National Institutes of Health to evaluate if a coping skills training (CST) intervention will result in improved health 
status and quality of life as well as reduced mortality and hospitalizations compared with a heart failure education 
