costing Centers for Medicare and Medicaid Services (CMS) over $17 billion in Medicare expenditures in 2009. The Hospital
Readmissions Reduction Program (HRRP) empowers CMS to reduce hospital reimbursements based on 30-day readmissions 
prompting hospitals to increase their focus on readmission rate reduction.Purpose: This project investigated the impact 
of implementing post-discharge follow-up teach-back telephone calls, compared to usual care, on 30-day readmission rates
among HF patients (age> 65 years) in a large urban hospital system within the state of Illinois.Theoretical Framework: 
Orem’s theory of self-care deficit (1971) was used to design an educational intervention aimed at improving patients' 
post-discharge self? care, while Imogene King’s theory of goal attainment (1971) was used to enhance 
provider-participant instructional engagement. The project was implemented based on the Iowa model.ProQuest

INSTRUCTIONS: Based on the selection criteria above, decide whether this study should be INCLUDED or EXCLUDED. Provide a
brief rationale tied to specific criteria.


Out: None
