The study is excluded because it does not meet the intervention and comparison criteria of the systematic review. The 
review protocol specifies mHealth-delivered education interventions, such as internet/web-based education programmes, 
smartphone/tablet apps providing education, SMS education, or social media-delivered education. The study evaluated a 
telemedicine medication reminder system (an electronic pill box) and an m-health smartphone app for improving medication
adherence. There was no educational component; the intervention solely focused on reminding participants to take 
medications, not on delivering health education about heart failure. Therefore, it fails the intervention criterion.

Additionally, the review requires a comparison against usual heart failure care. The study used a 2×2 factorial design 
comparing different reminder conditions (pillbox silent, pillbox reminding, smartphone silent, smartphone reminding). 
There was no usual care control group; all participants received some form of device. Thus, the comparison condition is 
not met.

