effective in Western countries. However, it is not known whether they improve outcomes in a high population density     
country with a national health insurance programme. METHODS In total, 349 patients hospitalized because of heart failure
were randomized into control and MDP groups. All-cause death and re-hospitalization related to heart failure were       
