computer-based educational programme, not mHealth-delivered education. mHealth requires mobile and wireless technologies
(e.g., smartphone/tablet apps, SMS, social media), which are absent from the intervention description. Therefore, it 
does not satisfy the intervention criterion.", "confidence": "high"}]}
