contributing to effectiveness across interventions. This research aimed to develop and test a theory-linked taxonomy of 
generally applicable behavior change techniques (BCTs). DESIGN Twenty-six BCTs were defined. Two psychologists used a   
5-page coding manual to independently judge the presence or absence of each technique in published intervention         
descriptions and in intervention manuals. RESULTS Three systematic reviews yielded 195 published descriptions. Across 78
reliability tests (i.e., 26 techniques applied to 3 reviews), the average kappa per technique was 0.79, with 93% of     
