technique correspondence rate of 74%, with most mismatches (73%) arising from identification of a technique in the      
manual but not in the article. CONCLUSIONS These findings demonstrate the feasibility of developing standardized        
definitions of BCTs included in behavioral interventions and highlight problematic variability in the reporting of      
intervention content."                                                                                                  
